Airport Runway Scheduling
    Uses itertools.product to pair flights with runways.
    Uses collections.Counter to count how many flights each runway handles.
    Prints allocation schedule for flights → runways.
    Highlights when a runway reaches capacity.
    Summarizes runway usage and identifies the busiest runway.


Bruteforce Demo
    Simulates a password brute-force attack.
    Uses itertools.product to generate all possible 3-character passwords from a given character set.
    Compares each guess with the target password.
    Uses collections.Counter to track the number of attempts.
    Stops once the correct password is found and shows total attempts required.


Call Center
    Models a shift rotation system for call center agents.
    Uses itertools.cycle to rotate agents across multiple shifts and days.
    Uses collections.defaultdict to store each agent’s assigned shifts.
    Uses collections.Counter to count how many shifts each agent has worked.
    Prints a shift schedule and identifies the busiest agent.


Sports Tournament
    Creates a round-robin tournament schedule.
    Uses itertools.combinations to generate all possible team matchups.
    Uses collections.Counter to count how many matches each team plays.
    Prints the complete match schedule.
    Displays which team is most active in terms of match count.


Traffic Light Timer
    Simulates a traffic light cycle.
    Uses itertools.cycle to repeatedly loop through Red → Green → Yellow.
    Uses collections.deque to store and replay a sequence of light states.
    Uses collections.Counter to count how often each light appears in the simulation.
    Prints the light sequence and shows which light appears most frequently.